There are several ways to terminate a C program:

1. Using the return statement: You can use the return statement to terminate a function and return a value to the calling function. If used outside of a function, it will terminate the entire program.

```c
int main() {
    // Your code here
    return 0;
}
```

2. Using the exit() function: The exit() function is provided by the standard library and can be used to terminate the program immediately. It takes an integer status code as an argument, which is returned to the calling environment.

```c
#include <stdlib.h>

int main() {
    // Your code here
    exit(0);
    return 0;
}
```

3. Using the return key: In some cases, you can simply press the return key after entering the last line of your code. This will automatically terminate the program, but it is not recommended for production code.

```c
int main() {
    // Your code here
    return 0;    // Press the return key here
}
```

